sections.body:
- `src/slicer/graph.py`: `ranked_order` ranks named keys in this order:
  - version-shaped keys first, by version ascending (`v1.2` before `v1.10`, a bare `v1` before `v1.1`, as `render._version_parts` compares them), whether or not they are declared; equal versions keep `pass_keys()` order;
  - then the other non-empty keys in `pass_keys()` order (declared, then undeclared), as the renderer places them after the versions.
  Empty keys still merge by effective score against the next named row. Ascending still reverses the whole order. Readiness groups still come first.
- Move `_VERSION_KEY` and `_version_parts` out of `render.py` to one place both modules import (`model.py` beside `pass_keys`, or `graph.py`), so render and ranking cannot disagree on what a version is. Render output is unchanged.
- Docs that state the old rule, each reworded to the new one:
  - `docs/commands.md`, the `list` row (drop "Pass labels are not parsed as versions…" and say version-shaped keys rank by version, then other keys in declaration order);
  - `docs/agents.md` (the `list` row and the `next` paragraph near "declared pass order, descending effective score");
  - `docs/getting-started.md` (the default `list` paragraph);
  - `docs/tui.md` (the queue order paragraph);
  - `CHANGELOG.md` under Changed.
- `tests/test_list_pass_order.py`.
